Just wondering - it it a bug, a minor omission, a feature or
whatever? A character wearing cursed gloves cannot put on a ring
however an incubus can still put a ring of adornment on one's hand
_before_ he tries to remove gloves (which may be unsuccessful).

To a certain extent, that can be explained as intended (or at least
not entirely incorrect) behaviour. Apparently, when a glove-wearing
character puts on or removes rings it is assumed that she silently
removes and puts on gloves, the message only appears if the operation
is impossible because the gloves are cursed. Also apparently, incubus
has to do the same when fiddling with character's rings AND incubus
has the power to remove cursed armor so he should be able to perform
the gloves off - ring on - gloves back on operation without any extra
comments. Still, it feels a bit strange to find a ring under cursed
gloves after the encounter...

Interestingly, wiki says that incubus will honor cursed weapon status
when choosing what hand to put the ring on. It can still be assumed
that foocobi, compared, say, to nymphs, are only known to be able to
remove armor and not anything else but this limitation sounds a bit
funny. I wonder what they do if the cursed weapon is two-handed,
should probably try some wizmode experimenting.

The described case doesn't seem to appear on the official bug list, so
what do you think?


